{
  "body_human_readable": "### \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" Finances: A Look at the Film's Budget and Box Office Performance\n\nThe 2005 film adaptation of Douglas Adams' beloved science fiction comedy, \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,\" was produced with a budget estimated between $45 and $50 million. The movie went on to gross approximately $104.5 million worldwide.\n\nThe film, which stars Martin Freeman as the perpetually bewildered Arthur Dent, opened in the United States on April 29, 2005, with a weekend gross of about $21.1 million. Domestically, the movie earned a total of $51.1 million, accounting for roughly 49.7% of its worldwide total.\n\nFinancially, the worldwide box office return was about 2.3 times its production budget. While the film received a mix of reviews from critics, it grossed over $100 million globally.",
